<title>UK: Northern Electric resumes trade, holds firm.</title>
<headline>Northern Electric resumes trade, holds firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Electric said trading in its shares had resumed from 0820 GMT on Tuesday after the conclusion of an appeal process by the Panel on Takeovers and Mergers.</p>
<p>Northern Electric opened at 645 pence, up from its last price of 641 on Friday, December 20.</p>
<p>The UK utility is fighting a 782 million stg hostile takeover bid from CE Electric of the U.S. The deadline for acceptances is 1300 GMT today.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
